(RURAL WATER SUPPLY DEPARTMENT — Tender CE/ELE/60/2026-27) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. The quality of treated water shall comply with IS 10500:2012.) Tj T*
(2. The pH value of treated water shall lie within 6.5 to 8.5.) Tj T*
(3. TDS of treated water shall be limited to 500 mg per litre.) Tj T*
(4. The turbidity of treated water shall be limited to 5 NTU..) Tj T*
(5. Fluoride \(as F\) shall be limited to 1.0 mg per litre.) Tj T*
(6. Nitrate \(as NO3\) shall be limited to 45 mg per litre.) Tj T*
(7. Arsenic \(as As\) shall be limited to 0.01 mg per litre.) Tj T*
(8. Total hardness \(as CaCO3\) shall be limited to 200 mg per litre.) Tj T*
(9. No E. coli shall be detected in any 100 ml sample.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 6: TESTING, INSPECTION AND CERTIFICATION) Tj T*
(1. Works testing of the pumps shall be done as per IS 9137.) Tj T*
(2. Each motor shall be subjected to routine tests as per IS 4029.) Tj T*
(3. All motors shall carry the ISI mark.) Tj T*
(4. Testing of water samples shall be done at a NABL accredited laboratory as per IS 3025) Tj T*
(and IS 1622.) Tj T*
(5. Before despatch, the Engineer-in-charge will inspect the equipment at the maker's) Tj T*
(works.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7 DOCUMENTATION, WARRANTY AND TRAINING) Tj T*
(1. The contractor shall submit test reports for every source to the Engineer-in-charge.) Tj T*
(2. Detailed shop drawings are to be submitted by the contractor for approval not later) Tj T*
(than 21 calendar days after the award of work.) Tj T*
(3. On completion the contractor shall hand over three copies of the O&M manuals.) Tj T*
(4. The contractor shall guarantee the whole installation for 12 months after handing) Tj T*
(over against faulty design, materials and workmanship.) Tj T*
(5. Operation and routine maintenance training shall be given by the contractor to the) Tj T*
(Department's operators.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Signature of Bidder) Tj T*
(Page 3 of 5) Tj T*
ET
